pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `Cardinality::substitute`, which lowers the degree with an unchecked `-= 1` per literal mapped
% to TRUE. `1 x1 1 x2 >= i64::MIN` has all coefficients one and a degree that fits `i64`, so
% `into_smallest_type()` stores it as a cardinality constraint and the general-PB fix alone
% would not cover it.
f 2;
rup 1 x1 1 x2 >= -9223372036854775808 ;
red 1 ~x1 >= 1 : x1 -> 1 ;
pol 1 4 +;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
